    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="0851" n="841" xml:id="pg841"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.6336/11–3048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-30T16:00:00+08:00">November 30,
                            1948—4 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 1—4:09 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1275. We have heard nothing from Mukden since Communists closed transmitter but
                    assume he has been attempting communicate with outside world. Since his efforts
                    apparently fruitless, Department may wish to instruct either Moscow or Dairen to
                    make an approach to Soviet authorities to ascertain his welfare.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
